WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.400
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.734
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.968
Thank you.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.901
Thank you for watching.
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.734
Well guys, today CNN officially
launched their brand new

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:16.601
streaming service, CNN Plus.
That's right.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:21.167
With CNN Plus can you get news
from CNN all day at any time.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:29.133
Or, as that's also known, CNN.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.567
But CNN is actually trying to
reach a younger audience

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.801
with their streaming service,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.100
which explains why one show is
just Wolf Blitzer

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.834
playing Fortnite for an hour.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.534
That's right, CNN Plus
officially launched today.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:41.868
That's right,
a whole streaming service

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.601
filled with CNN shows
and footage.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.367
Check out some of the slogans
that they're testing out

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.801
to get people on board.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.767
First, up there's "CNN Plus,
the airport bar experience

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:55.200
right on your phone."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.901
That's the only place I ever see
that and I go,

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.200
"Wow, that's a great show."
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.300
Next up there's "CNN Plus,
the most trusted name

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.300
in news, according to CNN.com"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.334
You said that?

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.667
And finally, there's
"CNN Plus,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.334
your daily dose of anxiety,
now on mobile."

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:17.734
[ Laughter and applause ]
Ugh! Oh, gosh! Send.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.767
Let's switch gears. Guys,
everyone's talking about this.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.934
The house committee
investigating the Capitol riot,

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:26.901
said that Trump's White House
phone records have a 7-hour gap

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:30.868
on January 6th.
Seven hours.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.434
I don't know if anyone else is a
fan of the show "Dateline,"

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:37.067
but if your phone records are
missing even 10 minutes,

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.167
you're guilty.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:41.701
That's just --
"between 9:45 and 9:55,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.834
Terrence didn't answer
his phone."

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.467
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.634
"He said he was taking a nap

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.334
that he always takes,
every night."

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.200
[ Light laughter ]
"At 9:45."

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.100
The only time there should be
a seven hour gap

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.334
is when you're trying to
remember what happened

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:57.734
on St. Patrick's day.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:02.400
You put on a Dr. Seuss hat,
got on the train.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.100
Yep, seven hours are missing,
yeah.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.667
Even the ghost of Richard Nixon
is like,

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:11.367
"I don't think can you do that."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.534
And now after making the
discovery the house committee

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:17.334
is investigating whether Trump
used burner phones.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.133
It's always reassuring when a
president acts like

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.133
a character in "The Wire."
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.868
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.367
Seriously, were they planning
an insurrection

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.834
or selling weed
to high school kids?

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:29.300
I don't -- I don't know which.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.267
Meanwhile, after
President Biden's recent remark

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.234
that Putin cannot remain
in power,

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.467
a reporter asked Biden
if he thinks his comments

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:38.400
can cause Putin to escalate
his behavior.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.467
Yeah, 'cause up until now Putin
has kept things pretty chill,

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.501
I think.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.267
I don't think anything
Biden says

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.734
is gonna change what Putin does.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.868
It's like shouting to
a lion at the zoo.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.133
It doesn't care
what you're saying.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.734
If the lion can
get over that fake river,

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:56.234
you're going to get mauled.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.534
Some business news.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.667
Fedex just announced
that after more than 50 years,

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:02.701
its founder and CEO
is stepping down.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.100
[ Audience aws ]
Yep.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.534
On his last day
he'll be driven home

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:07.100
and then thrown
on to his front lawn.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:11.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:17.534
[ Rim shot ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:21.400
-Hey!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.934
-Of course he doesn't
want to lose touch,

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.601
so he gave all his coworkers his
tracking number, which is nice.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.601
[ Laughter ]
You know where he is.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.200
He's in Wisconsin right now,
he'll be home soon.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.634
You gotta see this.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.834
Apparently Verizon customers
have been receiving spam texts

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.901
from their own phone numbers.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.167
It's weird when you get a text
from yourself at 2:00 a.m.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:44.767
that says "Me up?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.267
Meanwhile,
AT&amp;T customers are like,

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.667
"Ha ha,
that's what you get

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.434
for a company that has cell
service."

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:58.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.434
Hey, listen to this.

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:05.767
I read that avocado prices have
skyrocketed to a 24-year high.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.133
Man, did I pick the wrong time
to enjoy gasoline

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:11.100
over my avocado toast.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.734
Everything about it feels wrong.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.100
Yep.
Everyone is looking for cheaper

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.467
options which explains this new
jingle I saw today.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.501
♪ Avocados from
New Jersey ♪

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:23.300
There you go, 'ey!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.501
"I got your avocados
right here."

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.367
-"A couple of 'em, 'ey."

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:32.200
-And finally, police say the
general manager of a Denny's

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.367
in Pennsylvania embezzled over
$200,000 from the restaurant.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:37.567
[ Audience ohs ]
It's serious.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.167
If charged,
the manager could face 10 years

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.067
in the grand slammer.
There you go--

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.300
[ Laughter ]
We have a great show.

